        "en": "The steel and metals sector represents a classic materials industry spanning mining, steelmaking, rolling and processing, and is highly cyclical and sensitive to global price cycles. On the Korean market, the sector includes a large number of listed names, but individual market capitalizations tend to be modest, keeping the sector's overall market weight limited. Within the sector, however, non-ferrous smelter Korea Zinc stands out with an outsized scale that gives the group an unusual composition, while the remainder consists of flat and long steel producers led by Hyundai Steel alongside copper-alloy and aluminum foil processors such as Poongsan and Sam-A Aluminum. Supplying materials to a wide range of downstream industries including automotive, shipbuilding, construction and electronics, the sector also functions as a barometer for Korea's broader manufacturing cycle. Recently, structural oversupply from China and expanding low-price exports have emerged as a common risk weighing on overall conditions."
