        "en": "At the upstream end of the value chain, smelting and non-ferrous metal producers Korea Zinc and Younpoong process ore into zinc, lead, gold and silver for supply to the electronics, automotive parts and battery materials industries. In the midstream, blast-furnace and electric-arc-furnace producers of flat and long products—Hyundai Steel, KG Steel, Dongkuk Steel and Hankuk Steel—manufacture steel for construction, automotive and shipbuilding applications. Specialty steel and steel pipe makers such as SeAH Steel and Kiswire supply energy and infrastructure pipes and wire rope, while downstream processing is represented by Poongsan, which produces copper-alloy and defense materials, and Sam-A Aluminum, which manufactures aluminum foil for batteries and electronic materials. Market capitalization within the sector is heavily concentrated in the single name Korea Zinc, resulting in an unusually high degree of top-name concentration compared with other sectors, while the remaining listed companies form a fragmented, multi-product but individually small-scale structure."
