        "en": "Looking ahead, the key focus across both platform and SI companies is whether AI monetization materializes into tangible results. NAVER has begun introducing advertising into its AI Briefing feature since July to capture search advertising revenue, with monetization of its AI Tab planned for the fourth quarter, meaning near-term share price direction is likely to hinge on the visible progress of AI monetization. Additionally, some analysts suggest that as the AI Factory business structure developed with global partners such as NVIDIA takes shape and cloud infrastructure revenue becomes more visible, valuation could be reassessed. Among SI providers, expansion into new business areas such as finance, robotics, and global markets, alongside securing profitability, is emerging as a key variable determining future outcomes, with LG CNS in particular presenting physical AI, financial AX, and GPU infrastructure as its three growth pillars. For Kakao, proving the commercial viability of its KakaoTalk-centered AI agent business remains a core challenge, and each company's progress on AI transformation is widely viewed as the primary variable that will determine potential re-rating at both the individual stock and sector level."
