        "en": "The bio-pharma sector encompasses a wide range of business models, from finished drug manufacturing and sales to contract development and manufacturing organizations (CDMO), biosimilars, and out-licensing of new drug pipelines. While the number of listed companies is very large, market capitalization is structurally concentrated in a small number of top firms, with Samsung Biologics and Celltrion together accounting for an overwhelming share of the sector. Within the Korean market, this sector is emerging as a major export contributor second only to semiconductors, with government statistics also showing steady growth in bio-health exports. Within Korea's pharma and bio industry, CDMO and biosimilars are the segments with the highest export share, and bio-health exports in June 2026 rose 14.1% year on year. At the individual company level, earnings and share price volatility tend to be high depending on R&D outcomes or the success of licensing deals, making it important to distinguish overall sector trends from company-specific issues."
