        "en": "Samsung Biologics and Celltrion have both posted record quarterly earnings in 2026. Celltrion achieved second-quarter sales of 1.39 trillion won and operating profit of 451.8 billion won, up 45% and 86.3% year on year respectively, marking consecutive record quarterly sales. Samsung Biologics also posted sales of 1.32 trillion won and operating profit of 586.4 billion won, maintaining a 44.4% operating margin despite initial costs from its new fifth plant and Rockville facility. Among platform-technology biotechs, Alteogen's Hybrozyme-based subcutaneous injection technology has entered commercialization and is translating into earnings. Sales of the subcutaneous Keytruda formulation surged 262% from $128 million in Q1 to $463 million in Q2, and Alteogen's own Q2 sales jumped 269.5% year on year. Yuhan Pharm continues to show quarterly earnings volatility tied to the expanded U.S. approval of Leclaza (Rybrevant) and milestone recognition timing, with potential milestone income from the European launch of the Rybrevant-Lazcluze combination and expected gradual growth in royalty income as combination prescriptions expand. Overall, K-bio out-licensing activity has been notably active."
