        "en": "The transportation and logistics sector spans container, bulk, tanker, and LNG shipping companies; integrated logistics firms serving automakers and affiliated e-commerce volumes; land transport operators in parcel delivery, port cargo handling, and intercity bus services; and specialized players such as subsea cable installation and car-sharing. While its overall weight in the Korean equity market is modest, the sector carries outsized strategic importance as it is directly tied to national trade volumes. The sector comprises more than twenty listed names, but the size distribution is highly skewed, with market capitalization concentrated in a handful of leaders. Container and bulk carriers have earnings directly linked to global freight indices such as the SCFI and BDI, making them cyclical, whereas captive logistics providers tend to show lower earnings volatility thanks to stable affiliate-driven cargo volumes. A notable recent trend is that ocean carriers are diversifying away from single-segment container exposure into bulk, tanker, and LNG operations."
