        "en": "The value chain can be broadly divided into four stages: artist planning and development (HYBE, SM Entertainment, JYP Entertainment, YG Entertainment), fandom platforms and distribution (Dear U, SOOP, and HYBE's Weverse), content production and distribution (CJ ENM, Studio Dragon), and exhibition and advertising (CJ CGV, Cheil Worldwide, Innocean). The upstream planning and development stage directly holds neighboring rights and artist IP, capturing comprehensive revenue streams from albums, concerts, merchandise, and platforms, with HYBE holding a scale advantage at this stage through its multi-label strategy encompassing numerous groups. Cheil Worldwide and Innocean, the advertising agencies, secure relatively stable captive revenue based on affiliated volumes from the Samsung and Hyundai Motor Group conglomerates respectively, resulting in comparatively lower earnings volatility within the sector. At the content production and distribution stage, CJ ENM and Studio Dragon generate revenue by supplying drama content to domestic and overseas OTT platforms, while CJ CGV operates multiplex cinema businesses both domestically and abroad in Vietnam, Indonesia, and Turkey. Sector concentration is heavily skewed toward a handful of top agencies in terms of market capitalization, with the larger number of smaller names having limited influence on the overall sector landscape given their smaller individual IP or business scale."
