        "en": "The value chain is broadly divided into design and engineering, hull construction, engine and equipment installation, and post-delivery service (MRO). The three major shipyards—HD Hyundai Heavy Industries, Hanwha Ocean, and Samsung Heavy Industries—build merchant ships such as LNG carriers, container ships, and tankers alongside offshore plants and special-purpose naval vessels, accounting for most of the sector's revenue, while HD Korea Shipbuilding & Offshore Engineering functions as an intermediate holding company overseeing shipbuilding affiliates. Downstream, marine engine suppliers include Hanwha Engine, HD Hyundai Marine Engine, and STX Engine, while Sejin Heavy Industries and Hyundai Hims handle blocks and other shipbuilding equipment. HD Hyundai Marine Solution operates in vessel services and MRO, while Daehan Shipbuilding is a small-to-mid-sized yard specialized in specific vessel types such as tankers. Market capitalization within the sector is concentrated in the top three shipbuilders and HD Hyundai Marine Solution, meaning the conditions facing a handful of leading names largely drive the sector's overall trajectory."
